+---
+# 0012: Gate shrink (Top 10 #4b) and `--via` removal
+
+**Context.** The conductor gate grew to 552 lines (analyst plan `.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md` §2). Replaying 881 conductor Bash calls from 8 transcripts (2026-10-18..10-28, §3) gave 754 allowed and 127 denied. Used: `harness`, `cat`/`ls`, `git log|status|diff --stat|branch`, `gh pr create|merge|view|edit|list|comment|checks`, `herdr pane current|get`. Never used: `git show --stat`; `herdr status`, `pane list|layout`, `workspace|tab list`; `gh issue|run|repo|auth|browse|pr status`; `jq` as a pipe consumer (0 allowed). 44 of 754 calls chained with `;`/`&`, 0 piped, 0 used `2>&1`. No filesystem MCP server is configured. The B′ spike (native subagents instead of the harness runner) was rejected on 2026-11-03 (`.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md`): subagents die when the conductor exits ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped"), so the runner and therefore the gate stay.
+
+**Decision.** Keep the gate and trim it by usage, as planned in gate-shrink-detail §6:
+- (a) one simple command per call, quote-aware scanner instead of a segment splitter (commit 4d9b627, gate v21; wiki: conductor-shell-one-command); (g) the gate keys on hook `agent_type`; the regression list `tests/gate-denied.list` drives a test loop.
+- (b) tool-name denies (Agent, Workflow, Monitor, NotebookEdit) live in `claude/agents/conductor.md` `disallowedTools`; the gate has no case for them, and the `mcp__filesystem__*` block is gone. The hook matcher is `Edit|Write|Read|Grep|Glob|Bash`.
+- (c) gh: only `pr create|view|list|checks|comment|edit|merge`; `--body-file`/`-F` only from `.harness/` or `docs/`; no `pr merge -d`; no `api`.
+- (d) git: `status`, `log`, `diff --stat`, and `git branch` followed only by `-a -r -v --show-current` (a regex, not a parser); herdr: `pane get|current` only.
+- (e) policy tables (`BASH_ALLOW`, `GH_ALLOW`, `GIT_DENY`, messages) sit in one block at the top, after the prologue.
+- `--via` is removed from `harness ask`; it is now an unknown option (exit 1, logged as a usage error).
+- Kept on purpose: the path helpers (`rel`, `physrel`, `physical`, readable/writable, raw-stream rule; ~109 lines) are the core protection against symlink and raw-stream leaks, and the Bash allowlist is what stops `python3`, `sed`, `herdr pane run`. A 50-line gate is not possible without dropping them.
+- Rejected, option (f), `permissions` rules instead of the gate: user-scope `permissions` live in the same settings file that workers use, so they bind workers too; deny beats allow, so "deny Read except .harness/docs" cannot be written; Bash patterns are fragile. Only tool-name denies are possible, and (b) already covers them.
+
+**Status.** Active. Supersedes the "shrink toward permissions rules" consequence of [0005](0005-gate-only-inside-herdr.md) (4b).
+
+**Consequences.** Gate: 552 lines (analysis) → 513 now; step 5 itself changed no gate lines because (a), (b)-(e), (g) had already landed (v21), and added one gate test per form listed under "You may run directly" in conductor.md. Chained commands must be separate parallel calls. A new MCP server that reads files is not gated (add it to `disallowedTools`). Old progress rows may carry a `via` field; nothing reads it.
